          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Simplify the following expressions, then differentiate ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "without",
              "marks": [
                "italic"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " using the product rule.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-group-23-26-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=\\dfrac{x^{2}+4x+4}{\\sqrt{x+2}}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=(x+2)^{3/2}$; $y'=\\dfrac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x+2}$. \n\nFactor the numerator, then use the chain rule.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\dfrac{(x+2)^2}{\\sqrt{x+2}}\\\\y&=(x+2)^{3/2}\\\\y'&=\\dfrac{3}{2}(x+2)^{1/2}\\\\y'&=\\dfrac{3}{2}\\sqrt{x+2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-group-23-26-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=x^{3}\\left(x+\\dfrac{2}{x}\\right)^{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=(x^{2}+2)^{3}$; $y'=6x(x^{2}+2)^{2}$. \n\nCombine the factors before applying the chain rule.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\left[x\\left(x+\\dfrac{2}{x}\\right)\\right]^3\\\\y&=(x^2+2)^3\\\\y'&=3(x^2+2)^2(2x)\\\\y'&=6x(x^2+2)^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-group-23-26-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=(x+3)\\sqrt{4x+12}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=2(x+3)^{3/2}$; $y'=3\\sqrt{x+3}$. \n\nFactor the radicand, then use the chain rule.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=(x+3)\\sqrt{4(x+3)}\\\\y&=2(x+3)^{3/2}\\\\y'&=2\\cdot\\dfrac{3}{2}(x+3)^{1/2}\\\\y'&=3\\sqrt{x+3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-group-23-26-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=(x^{2}+4x+4)\\sqrt{x+2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=(x+2)^{5/2}$; $y'=\\dfrac{5}{2}(x+2)^{3/2}$. \n\nFactor the quadratic, then use the chain rule.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=(x+2)^2\\sqrt{x+2}\\\\y&=(x+2)^{5/2}\\\\y'&=\\dfrac{5}{2}(x+2)^{3/2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
